xgrammar and dlpack (inside libtfgrammar.so)
  https://github.com/mlc-ai/xgrammar (MLC-AI team), https://github.com/dmlc/dlpack (DLPack contributors). Apache License, Version 2.0.
  scripts/prepare.sh copies the prebuilt lib/libtfgrammar.so out of TensorFold's v1.1.4 release archive (aarch64, checked against its
  SHA-256 in scripts/config.sh) into /opt/tensorfold/native/lib, with the archive's xgrammar and dlpack license and notice files in
  /opt/tensorfold/share/doc/tensorfold/LICENSES-grammar. The library serves structured output and required tool calls; nothing of it is
  modified or compiled here.

Model files (downloaded from Hugging Face by scripts/prepare.sh; not included in this repository or its image)
  The checkpoint this recipe serves by default, nvidia/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-FP4-Local, is NVIDIA's quantization-aware-distilled
  FP4 export (NVIDIA Model Optimizer) of Qwen/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next by the Qwen team (Alibaba). Its use is governed by the NVIDIA Open
  Model Agreement (https://www.nvidia.com/en-us/agreements/enterprise-software/nvidia-open-model-agreement/); the base model is under the
  Qwen Community License 1.0 (https://huggingface.co/Qwen/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next/blob/main/LICENSE).
  The optional checkpoint (CHECKPOINT=int4, served by the db281878 recipe on main, not by this branch), azampatti/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-125B-A5B-INT4-AutoRound, is by azampatti (the
  top-5 expert cut and the shared-expert healing), built on Intel's AutoRound int4 quantization
  (Intel/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-W4A16-AutoRound) and on Saren-Arterius's hybrid checkpoint and FP8 n-gram table
  (Saren/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-ple-table-fp8), of Qwen/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next. Per its model card, it is under the Qwen license
  (https://huggingface.co/Qwen/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next/blob/main/LICENSE).

